<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Freedom Charter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Freedom Charter is the statement of principles adopted by the Congress of the People at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kliptown">Kliptown</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a> on 26 June 1955, organised by the ANC and its allies in the Congress Alliance. Opening with the words '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> belongs to all who live in it, black and white', it called for equal rights, a non-racial democracy and a fair share of the country's wealth. It led to the Treason Trial and became the core programme of the ANC.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/freedom-charter.jpg" alt="Freedom Charter" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joonasl · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kliptown_Freedom_Charter_Memorial_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
